Subject: [PATCH] agent: the main thread changes the shared data model under the command lock

The agent's one data model is shared by every node. The main thread added and deleted its station
rows with no lock: the analyze_* decoders write OneWifi's reports into it (an AP Metrics Report's
station info among them), and the orchestrator's pre-processing (pre_process_orch_op, outside the
command lock in submit_commands) applies the full-snapshot deltas, the station aggregate and the
link metrics, removing and deleting rows. Meanwhile a node built a Topology Response or an AP
Metrics Response walking m_sta_map, holding a row across several TLV builders: a row deleted
under it is a use-after-free, and the controller's usual answer to a station event (a Topology
Query) makes the two meet. The 1 s tick also re-armed and recovered radios' WSC states unlocked,
racing the radio's own transition.

With the nodes now handling everything under the command lock, the main thread takes it around
each event it handles (handle_event: the decoders, pre-processing and submission included) and
around the 1 s tick's WSC rearm and recovery. The lock is recursive, so the orchestrator taking it
again inside is unchanged; no main path waits for a node while holding it (the agent joins its
nodes only in its destructor; bus callbacks only queue). The cost is latency: a node's reply waits
while the main thread finishes an event, its bus calls included.
---
diff --git a/src/agent/em_agent.cpp b/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
index ad63beda..016d0978 100644
--- a/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
@@ -1842,6 +1842,17 @@ void em_agent_t::on_queue(em_event_t *queued)
 
 void em_agent_t::handle_event(em_event_t *evt)
 {
+    // The data model's station rows (m_sta_map, m_sta_dassoc_map), BSSs and radios change here:
+    // the analyze_* decoders write OneWifi's reports into the shared model, and the orchestrator's
+    // pre-processing (pre_process_orch_op: the full-snapshot deltas, the station aggregate, the
+    // link metrics) adds and deletes rows. The nodes read them under the command lock (proto_run),
+    // so the main thread changes them under it too: a node building a Topology Response or an AP
+    // Metrics Response never walks a row being deleted. The lock is recursive (submit_commands and
+    // handle_ready_commands take it again).
+    std::unique_lock<std::recursive_mutex> command_lock;
+    if (m_orch != NULL) {
+        command_lock = m_orch->lock_commands();
+    }
     // a command socket client's event answers that client (send_result), and only it
     if (m_agent_cmd != NULL) {
         m_agent_cmd->begin_reply(evt);
@@ -2014,6 +2025,12 @@ void em_agent_t::handle_2s_tick()
 void em_agent_t::handle_1s_tick()
 {
     poll_native_backhaul_request();
+    // the radios' WSC states change here (rearm, recovery): under the command lock, as a radio's
+    // own transitions are (proto_run), so neither side's write is lost to the other's
+    std::unique_lock<std::recursive_mutex> command_lock;
+    if (m_orch != NULL) {
+        command_lock = m_orch->lock_commands();
+    }
     if (m_onewifi_wsc_subdoc_active && ++m_onewifi_wsc_wait_ticks >= 5) {
         std::string ruid = m_onewifi_wsc_ruid;
         m_onewifi_wsc_subdoc_active = false;
